\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {12}{\ignorespaces Mitigation results on the 20 RQ1-mitigated cases. {\fontfamily  {pzd}\fontencoding  {U}\fontseries  {m}\fontshape  {n}\selectfont  \char 51}\,=\,mitigated (tool produced an actionable signal for the target bug), {\fontfamily  {pzd}\fontencoding  {U}\fontseries  {m}\fontshape  {n}\selectfont  \char 55}\,=\,not mitigated (tool was applicable but produced no signal), \textcolor {gray}{N/A}\,=\,out of scope (no applicable rule or type file, or execution infeasible). GPTScan's rule set does not target numeric logic errors, hence all cases are out of scope. NumScout entries marked $^{\dagger }$ were evaluated on a semantically-equivalent variant in which external library functions were rewritten as internal to bypass NumScout's library-placeholder limitation; see §\ref {sec:rq3} for details.}}{42}{table.caption.30}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:rq3-mitigation}{{12}{42}{Mitigation results on the 20 RQ1-mitigated cases. \ding {51}\,=\,mitigated (tool produced an actionable signal for the target bug), \ding {55}\,=\,not mitigated (tool was applicable but produced no signal), \textcolor {gray}{N/A}\,=\,out of scope (no applicable rule or type file, or execution infeasible). GPTScan's rule set does not target numeric logic errors, hence all cases are out of scope. NumScout entries marked $^{\dagger }$ were evaluated on a semantically-equivalent variant in which external library functions were rewritten as internal to bypass NumScout's library-placeholder limitation; see §\ref {sec:rq3} for details}{table.caption.30}{}}
